cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Running Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 on DGX Spark with vLLM MTP for Local Speed and Smarts Benchmarks"
message: "If you use this setup, benchmark wrappers, or comparison data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rawat"
    given-names: "Rajendra Singh"
    affiliation: "cogni.chat"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5017-1341"
repository-code: "https://github.com/airawatraj/dgx-spark-qwen38-super-agent"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight technical implementation and benchmarking suite for running
  unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 on NVIDIA DGX Spark through vLLM with native
  Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) speculative decoding. This repository documents
  the optimized Docker configuration with native tool-calling, 262K context,
  reproducible benchmark wrappers for speed, smarts (100/100 tool-eval), and
  arena-style throughput sweeps on Spark hardware.
keywords:
  - "Qwen"
  - "Qwen3"
  - "DGX Spark"
  - "vLLM"
  - "MTP"
  - "Speculative Decoding"
  - "AI Agents"
  - "NVFP4"
  - "Performance Benchmarking"
  - "Tool Calling"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
